.TH "INSPEKT\-A11Y" "1" "2026\-04\-16" "Inspekt 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
inspekt\-a11y \- Run combined accessibility audit with selected engines.
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]inspekt\f[R] \f[B]a11y\f[R] [\f[I]OPTIONS\f[R]]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Run combined accessibility audit with selected engines.
.PP
Runs the specified accessibility checkers in order and consolidates
results by WCAG Success Criterion, showing all engine outcomes for
comparison.
.PP
ENGINE SELECTION:
.PP
By default, runs all available engines: axe, eac, hcs.
Use \(enengines/\-e with comma\-separated names to select specific
engines.
.PP
Order matters: engines execute in the order specified, which may affect
results when scripts have side effects (e.g., DOM mutations).
.PP
This helps identify:
.IP \(bu 2
Issues caught by one tool but not others
.IP \(bu 2
Conflicting assessments between tools
.IP \(bu 2
Comprehensive coverage of WCAG criteria
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\f[B]\-e\f[R], \f[B]\(enengines\f[R], \f[I]TEXT\f[R]
Engines to run, comma\-separated (default: axe,eac,hcs).
Available: axe, eac, hcs, sia
.TP
\f[B]\(enlist\-engines\f[R]
List available accessibility engines and exit
.TP
\f[B]\(enlevel\f[R], \f[I][2a|2aa|2aaa|21a|21aa|22aa]\f[R]
WCAG conformance level to test (default: 21aa)
.TP
\f[B]\(enformat\f[R], \f[I][json|html]\f[R]
Output format: json (machine\-readable) or html (interactive report)
.TP
\f[B]\(entimeout\f[R], \f[I]FLOAT\f[R]
Timeout in seconds for each engine (default: 60)
.TP
\f[B]\(enshow\-passes\f[R]
Include WCAG criteria where all engines pass
.TP
\f[B]\(eninclude\-recommendations\f[R]
Include recommendations and best practices from all engines
.TP
\f[B]\(enshow\-badges\f[R]
Show unified badges on elements with issues (run in browser)
.TP
\f[B]\(eninteractive\f[R]
Make badges clickable with detailed popover information (requires
\(enshow\-badges)
.TP
\f[B]\(enall\-disagreements\f[R]
Show all disagreements instead of limiting to 10
.TP
\f[B]\(eninfo\f[R]
Show engine metadata, version info, and complete rule listing with ACT
alignment
.TP
\f[B]\-v\f[R], \f[B]\(enverbose\f[R]
Show detailed rule\-level tables for each engine
.TP
\f[B]\(enscoped\f[R], \f[I]TEXT\f[R]
Scope tests to specific elements.
Use `inspected' for the currently inspected element, or provide CSS
selectors (comma\-separated)
.TP
\f[B]\(enexclude\f[R], \f[I]TEXT\f[R]
Exclude elements from testing.
Can be comma\-separated selectors or multiple \(enexclude flags
(repeatable)
.TP
\f[B]\(enrule\f[R], \f[I]TEXT\f[R]
Test a single axe\-core rule by ID (only works with axe engine)
.TP
\f[B]\(endisable\-rule\f[R], \f[I]RULE_ID\f[R]
Disable specific rules by ID (axe engine only).
Supports comma\-separated values.
(repeatable)
.TP
\f[B]\(enenable\-rule\f[R], \f[I]RULE_ID\f[R]
Run ONLY these rules (axe engine only).
Supports comma\-separated values.
(repeatable)
.TP
\f[B]\(enpersistent\f[R]
Monitor and re\-run audit on each page navigation (press Ctrl+C to stop)
.TP
\f[B]\(enno\-compliance\-warning\f[R]
Suppress the warning about automated checker limitations
.TP
\f[B]\(ensummary\-only\f[R]
Show only summary, agreement, and disagreements (skip detailed WCAG
table)
.TP
\f[B]\-o\f[R], \f[B]\(enoutput\f[R], \f[I]PATH\f[R]
Save output to file (requires \(enformat)
.TP
\f[B]\(enno\-open\f[R]
Don\(cqt auto\-open the HTML report in the browser
.TP
\f[B]\(enheadless\f[R]
Run audit in headless Chrome (no browser extension required)
.TP
\f[B]\(enmirror\-session\f[R]
Mirror cookies/storage from live browser for authenticated pages
(implies \(enheadless)
.TP
\f[B]\(enurl\f[R], \f[I]TEXT\f[R]
URL to audit in headless mode (required with \(enheadless unless
\(enmirror\-session)
.SH EXAMPLES
.IP
.EX
inspekt a11y
inspekt a11y \-e axe
inspekt a11y \-e eac
inspekt a11y \-e axe,eac
inspekt a11y \-e eac,axe
inspekt a11y \-\-level 21aa
inspekt a11y \-\-format json
inspekt a11y \-\-format html
inspekt a11y \-\-show\-badges
inspekt a11y \-\-list\-engines
inspekt a11y \-e axe \-\-info
.EE
